*Extra note from the lab documents (not from the Study Notes PDF).*

**Watch out**: `cin >>` stops reading at **whitespace** (space, tab, enter).

```
char word[21];
string name;
cin >> word;          // type: Hello World
cin >> name;
```
`word` = `Hello`, and `World` stays in the buffer and goes straight into `name` without waiting for the user (Lab 4 C2).

To read a whole line use `cin.getline(word, 21)` (C-string) or `getline(cin, name)` (string).

